## Knowledge And Documentation

- Use `DOCS_INDEX.md` as the main routing layer.
- Use `DOCS_INDEX.full.md` only when compact routing is insufficient and you need raw captures, source cards, proof folders, or lower-level artifacts.
- Prefer linking to source-of-truth systems instead of copying them unless a local artifact is genuinely useful.
- Prefer updating an existing domain file over creating a duplicate.
- Delete or merge replaced material instead of leaving parallel versions around.
- For internal context about {{USER_NAME}}'s life, projects, accounts, relationships, or current situations, update source-linked domain notes under `vault/`.
- For external saved material such as X posts, articles, papers, videos, or Gists, use the knowledge layer in `vault/Knowledge/`.
- When {{USER_NAME}} says "save this" with a URL or artifact, use `[$llm-wiki]({{WORKSPACE_PATH}}/.agents/skills/knowledge/llm-wiki/SKILL.md)` to capture a raw source snapshot when feasible, create a compact source card, and update or create compiled pages only when they will be reusable.
- When {{USER_NAME}} asks a question that should be grounded in the knowledge base, read `DOCS_INDEX.md`, `vault/Knowledge/Knowledge.md`, and the relevant domain pages before answering; cite the vault pages you used with wikilinks.
- If {{USER_NAME}} drops a source or question into `vault/Knowledge/INBOX.md`, process it through the knowledge layer and mark the item handled. {{USER_NAME}} should not need to browse source cards or operations files to get an answer.
- For link policy and domain shape, follow `vault/Operations/Vault Structure.md`.

For routed markdown docs:
- include `summary`, `last_updated`, and `read_when` frontmatter
- refresh `last_updated` when materially updating the doc
- run `python3 scripts/build-docs-index.py` after creating or modifying routed docs

